 interview (2026-04-06) he said he would \"open up oil and gas production in California\".\n- **Why it can't be rung 4:** rung 4 is \"Expand fossil fuel production with new drilling and permits\". His words match it, but nothing he says either rules in or rules out rung 5, \"Maximize production and open more public land and waters to drilling\". The annex says a call for more drilling that doesn't exclude \"maximize\" is `direction-only`.\n- **\"As much as possible\":** this line in the CBS LA interview answers a question that isn't in the transcript. From the words that follow (\"we're going to need a lot of money\"), it seems to be about money from the oil industry, so I did not read it as \"maximize\".\n- **Campaign policy page:** the $3 gas page is written in the third person (\"Steve Hilton's plan\"). Under V1 that makes it someone else describing him, so it can't support a chair either way.\n- **The 2026-10-01 CBS LA clip:** it repeats the 2026-04-06 interview word for word, so I coded it as the same occasion, not a second source.\n- **Other passages:** the 2026-01-23 Commonwealth Club interview mentions oil and gas reserves but names no production policy (`adjacent`). The two CalMatters excerpts say nothing on fossil fuels (`not-evidence`).\n- **Quotes:**\n  - The CalGEM permits line and the \"open up oil and gas production\" plan line are coded `lever`, `lever-named`.\n  - The CNN \"opening up … production\" line and the \"let's use what we produce here\" line are coded `direction`.\n- **`needs_source`:**\n  - His own words on how far to expand, or on opening (or keeping closed) state lands, state waters or offshore areas.\n  - A first-person version of the $3 gas plan, or a questionnaire answer on oil and gas production.","ttft_ms":17169,"type":"result","duration_ms":55073,"uuid":"a42d1105-6fca-45e0-9cf1-f562b888f1ad","ttft_stream_ms":1307,"time_to_request_ms":78,"first_content_frame_ms":1308,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
